{"id":"jubilee","name":"Jubilee","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:jubilee"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Jubilee","text":"A joyful shout or clangour of trumpets, the name of the great semi-centennial festival of the Hebrews. It lasted for a year. During this year the land was to be fallow, and the Israelites were only permitted to gather the spontaneous produce of the fields (Lev. 25:11, 12). All landed property during that year reverted to its original owner (13-34; 27:16-24), and all who were slaves were set free (25:39-54), and all debts were remitted. The return of the jubilee year was proclaimed by a blast of trumpets which sounded throughout the land. There is no record in Scripture of the actual observance of this festival, but there are numerous allusions (Isa. 5:7, 8, 9, 10; 61:1, 2; Ezek. 7:12, 13; Neh. 5:1-19; 2 Chr. 36:21) which place it beyond a doubt that it was observed. The advantages of this institution were manifold. “1. It would prevent the accumulation of land on the part of a few to …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3104","lemma":"יוֹבֵל","xlit":"yôwbêl","gloss":"the blast of a horn","kjv":"jubile, ram's horn, trumpet","count":19,"share":0.32},{"strong":"H272","lemma":"אֲחֻזָּה","xlit":"ʼăchuzzâh","gloss":"something seized","kjv":"possession","count":15,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H4376","lemma":"מָכַר","xlit":"mâkar","gloss":"to sell, literally , or figuratively","kjv":"at all, sell","count":14,"share":0.24},{"strong":"H4465","lemma":"מִמְכָּר","xlit":"mimkâr","gloss":"merchandise","kjv":"ought, sale, that which...sold, ware","count":7,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H1353","lemma":"גְּאֻלָּה","xlit":"gᵉʼullâh","gloss":"redemption","kjv":"kindred, redeem, redemption, right","count":7,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H1350","lemma":"גָּאַל","xlit":"gâʼal","gloss":"to be the next of kin","kjv":"in any wise, at all, avenger, deliver","count":9,"share":0.15}],"verses":["Lev.25.10","Lev.25.11","Lev.25.12","Lev.25.13","Lev.25.15"